# Every text file is checked out with LF line ends, on every computer. The checks in scripts/ read pages such as
# builder.html with patterns that expect "\n" (as GitHub's Linux machines check them out); Git for Windows otherwise
# turns them into CRLF on the owner's computer and npm test fails there for no real reason. Binary files are found
# by Git itself and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
